# Squash solo - Ladder: Volleys
@description The volley in ten levels, from volleys close to the front wall to volleys from the
  short line, then the volley drop. Based on The Pursuit of Squash.
@speech rate 1.1
@minimum gap 0:00.8
@workout squash
@artwork ../images/squash.jpg
@include ../shared/squash.overtone

## Intro
Volley ladder: forehand and backhand, a step further from the front wall each level. Play the
chapter for your level and repeat it until you reach the target, then move on to the next. After a
miss, count from zero.

// The Pursuit of Squash, Forehand and Backhand Volley Solo Challenges levels 1 and 3 to 5 (level 2 is a
// technique video), then level 1 of the Volley Drop Solo Challenges as 6A and 6B. Each level moves the
// player further from the front wall.
## Level 1A: Forehand, close to the front wall
@ladder
Forehand, close to the front wall. Stand no more than two metres from the front wall, on your
forehand side, a metre or so off the side wall. Volley above the service line, and hit it again
before it touches the floor. A blue dot ball helps.
+0:00.7 Target: fifty without a break.
+0:00.7 Short punch. Racket up between hits.
+0:00.7 Soft. Keep it above the service line.

## Level 1B: Backhand, close to the front wall
@ladder
Backhand, close to the front wall. Stand no more than two metres from the front wall, on your
backhand side, a metre or so off the side wall. Volley above the service line, and hit it again
before it touches the floor. A blue dot ball helps.
+0:00.7 Target: fifty without a break.
+0:00.7 Racket high. Punch, then extend up.
+0:00.7 Firm wrist.

## Level 3A: Forehand, from halfway
@ladder
Forehand, from halfway. Tape on the floor halfway between the front wall and the short line. Stand
behind it on your forehand side, a metre or so off the side wall. Serve onto the front wall, then
volley the ball on your forehand, again and again without a bounce. A blue, red or single yellow dot
ball.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five without a break.
+0:00.7 Racket above the ball. Come down on it.
+0:00.7 Shoulders to the side wall.

## Level 3B: Backhand, from halfway
@ladder
Backhand, from halfway. Tape on the floor halfway between the front wall and the short line. Stand
behind it on your backhand side, a metre or so off the side wall. Serve onto the front wall, then
volley the ball on your backhand, again and again without a bounce. A blue, red or single yellow dot
ball.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five without a break.
+0:00.7 Racket high before the ball arrives.
+0:00.7 Shoulders to the side wall.

## Level 4A: Forehand, from three-quarters
@ladder
Forehand, from three-quarters. Move the tape three-quarters of the way from the front wall to the
short line. Stand behind it on your forehand side, serve onto the front wall, and keep volleying on
your forehand.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty without a break.
+0:00.7 More distance, same punch.
+0:00.7 Follow through to the front wall.

## Level 4B: Backhand, from three-quarters
@ladder
Backhand, from three-quarters. Tape three-quarters of the way from the front wall to the short line.
Stand behind it on your backhand side, serve onto the front wall, and keep volleying on your
backhand.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty without a break.
+0:00.7 More distance, same punch.
+0:00.7 Firm wrist. Extend up after contact.

## Level 5A: Forehand, from the short line
@ladder
Forehand, from the short line. Stand behind the short line on your forehand side. Serve onto the
front wall, and keep volleying on your forehand. This is where you volley in a match.
+0:00.7 Target: fifteen without a break.
+0:00.7 Firm enough to reach you, soft enough to control.
+0:00.7 Racket up between every volley.

## Level 5B: Backhand, from the short line
@ladder
Backhand, from the short line. Stand behind the short line on your backhand side. Serve onto the
front wall, and keep volleying on your backhand. This is where you volley the serve.
+0:00.7 Target: fifteen without a break.
+0:00.7 Firm enough to reach you, soft enough to control.
+0:00.7 Racket up between every volley.

## Level 6A: Forehand volley drop
@ladder
Forehand volley drop. Halfway between the front wall and the short line. Toss the ball up high to
yourself, then volley it short into the front right corner. Don't worry about technique yet: this is
for a feel of taking the ball in short.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty drops without a break, none in the tin.
+0:00.7 Soft hands. Open face.
+0:00.7 Want it harder? Make it bounce before the side wall.

## Level 6B: Backhand volley drop
@ladder
Backhand volley drop. Halfway between the front wall and the short line. Toss the ball up high to
yourself, then volley it short into the front left corner. Don't worry about technique yet: this is
for a feel of taking the ball in short.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty drops without a break, none in the tin.
+0:00.7 Soft hands. Open face.
+0:00.7 Want it harder? Make it bounce before the side wall.
